{
  "requirement": "The `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct agents not to raise mechanical changes to new text as questions. For text that was already agreed or that the user supplied, it MUST direct agents to show the change as a diff against that text, followed by a list of the mechanical changes.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement has two obligations on the bundled `habeas-requirements` skill:\n\n1. The skill must direct agents not to raise mechanical changes to new text as questions.\n2. For text that was already agreed or that the user supplied, the skill must direct agents to show the change as a diff against that text, followed by a list of the mechanical changes.\n\n`tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_requirements_skill_shows_mechanical_changes_without_asking]` is marked `{test}` for this requirement. It calls `assert_phrases(\"habeas-requirements\", ...)`, which builds the skill text from `fn[bundled_skill]` (`SKILL.md` plus its references, whitespace-collapsed). `fn[assert_text]` then asserts that the text contains each phrase and fails if one is missing. The test checks two phrases:\n\n- \"Show text that was already agreed or that the user supplied as a diff against that text, then a \\\"Mechanical:\\\" list of the changes\" covers obligation 2. It names both the already-agreed and user-supplied cases, the diff, and the \"Mechanical:\" list.\n- \"Don't raise mechanical changes to new text as questions\" covers obligation 1.\n\nBoth phrases appear in workflow step 4 of `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md`. The collapse step lets the phrase match across the file's line wraps.\n\nThe requirement constrains documentation text, so a phrase-presence assertion is the natural check. A change that dropped or reversed either directive would fail the test. Related tests, such as `fn[the_requirements_skill_shows_edits_outside_a_group_and_added_examples]`, add ordering checks, but they are not needed for adequacy. I found no untested obligation, no acknowledged gap, and no ambiguity.",
  "references": "13fedb8acef4f7fe7492cd2eb3e938861374f8650eaf71c5dee5f31438e8781c",
